["Which environmental factor can affect phenotype without changing DNA sequence?","Nutrition can influence growth and body size; this illustrates environmental effects on what?","Phenotype","Genotype always","Chromosome number always","Allele identity always","Environment can influence phenotype without altering genotype."],
["What is camouflage?","A moth's colour blending with tree bark is an example of what?","Camouflage","Courtship only","Pollination","Parasitism","Camouflage makes an organism less conspicuous in its environment."],
["What is mimicry?","A harmless species resembling a harmful species can illustrate what adaptation?","Mimicry","Osmosis","Respiration","Germination","Mimicry involves resemblance that can influence interactions with other organisms."],
["Which feature helps fish obtain oxygen from water?","What thin, highly vascular structures provide a large surface area for gas exchange in fish?","Gills","Lungs only","Stomata","Malpighian tubules","Gills exchange dissolved oxygen and carbon dioxide with water."],
["Which adaptation helps a cactus reduce water loss?","Which feature of many desert plants reduces transpiration?","Reduced leaves or spines","Very broad thin leaves","Permanently open stomata","Weak shallow roots only","Reduced leaf area and other xerophytic traits help limit water loss."],
["What is the ability to survive and reproduce in a particular environment related to?","In evolutionary biology, reproductive success in an environment is described as what?","Fitness","Body size alone","Age alone","Mutation rate only","Fitness is relative reproductive success in a given environment."]
