["Which practice helps conserve endangered species in their natural habitat?","Protecting a species within its native ecosystem is what type of conservation?","In-situ conservation","Ex-situ conservation only","Overhunting","Habitat fragmentation","In-situ conservation protects species in their natural habitats."],
["Which is an example of ex-situ conservation?","Keeping an endangered species in a carefully managed zoo or seed bank is what?","Ex-situ conservation","In-situ conservation","Deforestation","Poaching","Ex-situ conservation protects organisms outside their natural habitats."],
["What is sustainable use of a natural resource?","Using a resource at a rate that allows it to remain available for the future is called what?","Sustainable use","Overexploitation","Pollution","Habitat destruction","Sustainable use considers long-term availability and ecosystem health."],
["Which gas is a major greenhouse gas released by burning fossil fuels?","Carbon dioxide from fossil fuel combustion contributes to which environmental process?","Enhanced greenhouse effect","Ozone depletion only","Nitrogen fixation","Acid neutralisation","Carbon dioxide traps outgoing infrared radiation and contributes to warming."],
["Which action can reduce soil erosion on sloping farmland?","Planting cover crops and contour farming can help prevent what?","Soil erosion","Pollination","Genetic drift","Eutrophication directly","Vegetation cover and contour practices reduce runoff and soil loss."],
["What is poaching?","Illegal hunting or capture of wild animals is known as what?","Poaching","Domestication","Reforestation","Composting","Poaching is illegal hunting, capturing or killing of wildlife."]
